From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camera: keep software and manual control requests separate

The software exposure pass writes all controls, including zero-initialized
requests for controls it did not change. On an IMX363 this sets digital
gain to zero and attempts exposure zero. Apply only the selected adjustment,
using the observed value and sensor bounds, and leave neutral frames alone.

Refresh digital gain, initialize a selected camera's requests from its own
controls, and do not reapply stale manual requests during software AE/AF.
The process thread owns software adjustments; the IO thread applies manual
requests and hardware-auto mode switches. Preserve the current value when
switching a UI control into manual mode.

--- a/src/io_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/io_pipeline.c
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@
                         mp_camera_control_get_int32(&state_io.gain.control);
         }
 
